          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of an “
            %em> extension system
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#MarmolejoWood10"}> Marmolejo &amp; Wood (2010)
            ), originally called “
            %em>
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
              in extension form
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#Manes76"}> Manes (1976), p. 32
            ) and previously also referred to as a “
            %em>
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+triple"} Kleisli triple
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#Moggi91"}> Moggi (1991), Def. 1.2
            ) is an equivalent way of presenting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
            of a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            (on a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            (“iteration”) of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monads"} relative monads
            to the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+functor"} identity functor
          %p
            Specifically, noticing that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            may be understood as constructing its
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "algebra+over+a+monad#FreeAlgebras"} free algebras
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            of their
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying+sets"} underlying sets
          %blockquote
            %p#MarmolejoWoodQuote
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#MarmolejoWood10"}> Marmolejo-Wood 10
              \&amp;rbrack;: there is an important overarching reason to consider monads in this way. Extension systems allow us to completely dispense with the iterates
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              of the underlying arrow. No iteration is necessary. A moment’s reflection on the various terms of terms and terms of terms of terms that occur in practical applications suggest that this alone justifies the alternate approach.
              = succeed "\u2026" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              we note that extension systems in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher dimensional category theory
              provide an even more important simplication of monads. For even in dimension 2, some of the tamest examples are built on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctors"} pseudofunctors
              that are difficult to iterate.
          %p
            Major alternative motivation for extension systems comes from their understanding as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+triples"}> Kleisli triples
            ); see there for more.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            An
            %strong extension system
            (
            %a{:href => "#MarmolejoWood10"}> Marmolejo-Wood 2010
            ) on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\in C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A\in C
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi A
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A \colon A\to T A
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon B\to T A
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi T
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi T
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^T \colon T B \to T A
                (the
                %em Kleisli extension
                of
                = succeed ")," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    For every
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    we have
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi A
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi T
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mi T
                                %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\eta_A)^T = 1_{T A}
                %li
                  %p
                    For every
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                            %mi B
                            %mo →
                            %mi T
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon B\to T A
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mi T
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi η
                              %mi B
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^T \circ \eta_B = f
                %li
                  %p
                    For every
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi B
                          %mo →
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon B\to T A
                    and
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi g
                            %mo :
                            %mi C
                            %mo →
                            %mi T
                            %mi B
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:C \to T B
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mi T
                            %mo ∘
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mi T
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi f
                              %mi T
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi g
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi T
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^T \circ g^T = (f^T \circ g)^T
          %p
            Given these data, we make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi f
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T f = (\eta_A \circ f)^T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_A:T T A \to T A
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1_{T A})^T
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi η
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T,\eta,\mu)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi T
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^T = \mu_A \circ T f
            and check the above axioms. Thus, extension systems are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            to monads.
          %h3#the_kleisli_category The Kleisli category
          %p
            This presentation of a monad is especially convenient for defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_T
            (whence the aternative terminology “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+triple"}> Kleisli triple
            ”):
          %p
            its objects are those of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
            are the morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to T A
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:B\to T A
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:C \to T B
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi T
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^T \circ g
          %h3#the_category_of_algebras The category of algebras
          %p
            It is also possible to define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebras over a monad
            using this presentation. A
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                An object
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %li
              %p
                For every morphism
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi h
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to B
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi h
                          %mi B
                        %mo :
                        %mi T
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^B : T X \to B
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to B
                we have
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi h
                          %mi B
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %mi h
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^B \circ \eta_X = h
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:X\to B
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:Y\to T X
                we have
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi h
                          %mi B
                        %mo ∘
                        %msup
                          %mi y
                          %mi T
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi h
                          %mi B
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi y
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h^B \circ y^T = (h^B \circ y)^B
          %h3#strong_monads Strong monads
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong monad
            we simply have to enhance the extension operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^T
            to an internal morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T A)^B \to (T A)^{T B}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi B
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T B \times (T A)^B \to T A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+in+computer+science"} monad in computer science
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+monad"} relative monad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polymonad"} polymonad
          %h2#references References
          %p The notion appears explicitly in:
          %ul
            %li#Manes76
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernest+G.+Manes"}> Ernest G. Manes
              , Sec 3, Ex. 12 (p. 32) of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Theories
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-9860-1"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-9860-1
          %p and is expanded on considerably in
          %ul
            %li#MarmolejoWood10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"}> Francisco Marmolejo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+J.+Wood"} Richard J. Wood
              %em Monads as extension systems – no iteration is necessary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TAC"} TAC
              %strong 24
              4 (2010) 84-113 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/24/4/24-04abs.html"}> tac:24-04
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p An earlier appearance in a different guise (“devices”):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+F.+C.+Walters"}> R. F. C. Walters
              , Chapter I of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em A categorical approach to universal algebra
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/handle/1885/133321"} anu:1885/133321
          %p
            The use of extension systems (there called
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+triples"} Kleisli triples
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
            capturing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation"} computation
            with side effects is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Moggi91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugenio+Moggi"}> Eugenio Moggi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notions of computation and monads
              %strong 93
              1 (1991) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0890-5401(91)90052-4"}> doi:10.1016/0890-5401(91)90052-4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.disi.unige.it/person/MoggiE/ftp/ic91.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            This way of presenting a monad is also closely related to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuation-passing+style"} continuation-passing style
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrzej+Filinski"}> Andrzej Filinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Representing Monads
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.43.8213&rep=rep1&type=pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Generalization to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonads"} pseudomonads
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"}> Francisco Marmolejo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+J.+Wood"} Richard J. Wood
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kan extensions and lax idempotent pseudomonads
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TAC"} TAC
                %strong 26
                1 (2012) 1-29 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/26/1/26-01abs.html"}> 26-01
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"}> Francisco Marmolejo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+J.+Wood"} Richard J. Wood
                = succeed "," do
                  %em No-iteration pseudomonads
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TAC"} TAC
                %strong 28
                14 (2013) 371-402 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/28/14/28-14abs.html"}> tac:28-14
                \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
          %p
